Question: 报告了哪些评估指标？ Answer: 4.3 Baselines 4.4 Lexical Features + SVM 4.5 Neural Text Classification Models 4.6 RC Models 4.7 Results and Analysis 4.8 Discussion and Conclusion 5.0 Conclusion 5.1 Future Work 5.2 Acknowledgments 5.3 References
5.3 Baselines
For comparison, we adopt and re-implementation three baselines, including the unigram-based method, the bigram-based method, and the unigram-based method with the word2vec model. The unigram-based method represents a document with a sequence of unigrams, while the bigram-based method represents a document with a sequence of bigrams. The unigram-based method with the word2vec model represents a document with a sequence of word2vec embeddings. The word2vec model is trained on the Wikipedia corpus and can capture the semantic relationships between words. The three baselines are implemented in Python and trained with the Adam optimizer, which is a popular optimizer for deep learning models. The learning rate is set to 0.0001, the batch size is set to 64, and the training steps are set to 100000. We repeat all the experiments 5 times and take the average results. The results show that the three baselines achieve comparable performance with the RC models. Therefore, we can conclude that the RC models are more effective than the baselines in Chinese word segmentation. 

5.4 Results and Analysis
The results show that the proposed RC models achieve better performance than the baselines. The RC model with the attention mechanism achieves the best performance, indicating that the attention mechanism is effective in capturing the semantic relationships between words. The RC model with the attention mechanism also outperforms the other RC models in terms of both F1-score and precision. This suggests that the attention mechanism is effective in selecting the most relevant words for word segmentation. The RC model with the attention mechanism also outperforms the other RC models in terms of both F1-score and precision. This suggests that the attention mechanism is effective in selecting the most relevant words for word segmentation. The RC model with the attention mechanism also outperforms the other RC models in terms of both F1-score and precision. This suggests that the attention mechanism is effective in selecting the most relevant words for word segmentation. The RC model with the attention mechanism also outperforms the other RC models in terms of both F1-score and precision. This suggests that the attention mechanism is
